# The floor lever (#413): a 3/4 wooden block standing on the ground, an iron handle in a slot in its top, the knob.
# Active family (#236, Forest look card): the knob, the part you grab, is the walk-and-grab cue straw (`e1cfa5`, shade
# `c4b07e`), no red; the export gives the sheet the moon rim (D92, tools/moon_rim.py, RIM_OBJECTS) so the ink contour
# reads on the near-black play band of the layered forest.
# Frame "on" (handle leaning right) is frame 0, frame "off" (handle leaning left) is frame 1: the SpriteSheets.LEVER order.
# The base (rows 10-15) and the pivot (cols 7-8) are identical in both frames; row 15 rests on the floor line. The light
# comes from the upper left in both frames, so "off" is drawn, not mirrored.
size 16 16
color K 010000
color R e1cfa5
color D c4b07e
color Y e49620
color O dc9121
color B 985614
color b 7d430e
color d 5d2f06
color G 686666
color L a8a7a8
color g 464545
frame on
..........KKK...
.........KRRRK..
.........KRRDK..
.........KRDDK..
........KLgKKK..
........KLgK....
.......KLgK.....
.......KLgK.....
......KLgK......
......KLgK......
...KKKKLgKKKKK..
..KYYYdLgdYYYOK.
..KOYYYddYYYOOK.
..KBGBBBBBBGBdK.
..KbbbbbbbbbbdK.
..KKKKKKKKKKKKK.
frame off
...KKK..........
..KRRRK.........
..KRRDK.........
..KRDDK.........
..KKKLgK........
....KLgK........
.....KLgK.......
.....KLgK.......
......KLgK......
......KLgK......
...KKKKLgKKKKK..
..KYYYdLgdYYYOK.
..KOYYYddYYYOOK.
..KBGBBBBBBGBdK.
..KbbbbbbbbbbdK.
..KKKKKKKKKKKKK.
